0.0.0.0:0 -> 0.0.0.0
ok   netAddrFamily reads afInet back out of a v4 address
ok   a v4 address asks for 16 bytes
ok   netAddr4Bytes is that same 16
ok   the v4 family lands where this platform keeps it
ok   port 0 reads back as 0
255.255.255.255:65535 -> 255.255.255.255
ok   port 65535 survives the big-endian round trip
127.0.0.1:8080 -> 127.0.0.1:8080
ok   a v4 address does not render as a v6 one
:: (all zero) -> ::
ok   netAddrFamily reads afInet6 back out of a v6 address
ok   a v6 address asks for 28 bytes
ok   netAddr6Bytes is that same 28
ok   netAddrMaxBytes is the larger of the two
ok   the v6 family lands where this platform keeps it
::1:8080 -> [::1]:8080
ok   a v6 port is the same two bytes in the same place
ok   flowinfo is left zero
ok   scope_id is left zero
ok   the last group lands at byte 22, big-endian
2001:db8::1 -> 2001:db8::1
all ones -> ffff:ffff:ffff:ffff:ffff:ffff:ffff:ffff
one zero group -> 1:0:2:3:4:5:6:7
short run then long run -> 0:0:1::
two runs of two -> 1::2:0:0:3:4
trailing run -> 1::
a zeroed buffer -> af=0
ok   an unknown family takes sockaddr_in's length
